       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error. 8,500 mg three times daily comes to 25,500 mg/day. The usual maximum for metformin is about 2,550 mg/day (immediate-release), and that is 10 times higher. A dose that high risks severe lactic acidosis.\n\nDid you mean **850 mg** by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)? That is a standard strength and the maximum daily dose. Many clinicians start lower, for example 500 mg twice daily or 500 mg three times daily, and titrate up.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. I can also enter 850 mg PO TID with meals if you confirm that's what you meant."
